From 181949bd1193920d7a81fd82680c453e4506138f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:27:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0195: the codec's buck supply from the RPM, and the
 headphones

0194 on the phone: every stage of the speaker path powered and silent.
The WCD937x's buck and flyback, which feed all its outputs, run from
cdc-vdd-buck, pm6125 LDO14: an on-demand supply that Android's driver asks
the RPM for while it plays, and that nobody asked for here. A small RPM
client (mainline qcom_glink_rpm.c + smd-rpm.c: the message RAM FIFOs, the
APCS doorbell, an intentless rpm_requests channel) turns it on at 1.8 V.

The tone now also goes to the headphones (INT0/INT1 from RX2, CLSH_DSM_OUT,
-20 dB, SoundWire port 1 on lane 1 as swrm_port_config.h has it), and the
whole RX side runs in CLS_AB, the mode mixer_paths_bengal_idp.xml uses.
